From: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] hassio: unpack the baked images at build time (docker load --platform) (Odoo #2067)

Applies after 0131/0134. The bake's plain `docker load` of an armv7/aarch64 archive on the amd64
builder imported the compressed content only and committed NO containerd snapshot (BOSv1.6.0-rc13:
snapshot store empty, 15 images). Every device then unpacked each image at its first container
create / add-on install: Core 9 min 04 s of a ~15 min first boot, add-ons 35-72 s each.

- dind-import-containers.sh: `docker load --platform <board platform>` (armv7 -> linux/arm/v7,
  aarch64 -> linux/arm64, from /build/images.arch, an unknown arch fails the bake); fails the bake
  in the first minute when fewer snapshots than images are committed;
- hassio.mk: writes images.arch (BR2_PACKAGE_HASSIO_ARCH) next to images.expected.
The finished data.ext4 is judged by scripts/check-baked-snapshots.sh (VER-13; REPORT mode when this patch
was written, enforcing since the follow-up of 2026-11-16, see CHANGELOG).
---
  buildroot-external/package/hassio/dind-import-containers.sh | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
  buildroot-external/package/hassio/hassio.mk                 |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/buildroot-external/package/hassio/dind-import-containers.sh b/buildroot-external/package/hassio/dind-import-containers.sh
--- a/buildroot-external/package/hassio/dind-import-containers.sh
+++ b/buildroot-external/package/hassio/dind-import-containers.sh
@@ -16,12 +16,27 @@
 n_tar=0
 n_loaded=0
 
+# GA (Odoo #2067): UNPACK at build time. A plain `docker load` of a foreign-platform image
+# (armv7/aarch64 archive on an amd64 builder) only imports the compressed content and commits NO
+# containerd snapshot; the device then unpacks every image at its first container create / add-on
+# install (Core: ~9 min on the iHost, BOSv1.6.0-rc13). `docker load --platform` makes the daemon
+# unpack the layers for the board's platform now. The platform comes from the board arch
+# (hassio.mk: images.arch), never from the archive. Measured on docker 29.7.2, 29.8.2 and 29.9.3:
+# plain load = 0 snapshots, --platform load = committed snapshots. An unknown arch fails the bake.
+arch=$(cat /build/images.arch 2>/dev/null || echo "")
+case "${arch}" in
+	armv7)   platform=linux/arm/v7 ;;
+	aarch64) platform=linux/arm64 ;;
+	*) echo "GA dind-import: ERROR: /build/images.arch missing or unknown ('${arch}')" >&2; exit 1 ;;
+esac
+echo "GA dind-import: loading for ${platform} (unpacked at build time)"
+
 # Make sure to order images by size (largest first)
 # It seems docker load requires space during operation
 # shellcheck disable=SC2045
 for image in $(ls -S /build/images/*.tar 2>/dev/null); do
 	n_tar=$((n_tar + 1))
-	out=$(docker load --input "${image}")
+	out=$(docker load --platform "${platform}" --input "${image}")
 	echo "${out}"
 	if echo "${out}" | grep -q '^Loaded image'; then
 		n_loaded=$((n_loaded + 1))
@@ -35,6 +50,12 @@
 [ "${n_tar}" -eq "${expected}" ] || { echo "GA dind-import: ERROR: ${n_tar} archives, expected ${expected}" >&2; exit 1; }
 [ "${n_loaded}" -eq "${n_tar}" ] || { echo "GA dind-import: ERROR: ${n_loaded} of ${n_tar} archives loaded" >&2; exit 1; }
 
+# GA (Odoo #2067): the unpack must have happened -- fail here, in the first minute, rather than
+# after the whole build (scripts/check-baked-snapshots.sh judges the finished data partition).
+n_snap=$(ctr --address /var/run/docker/containerd/containerd.sock -n moby snapshots ls | tail -n +2 | wc -l)
+echo "GA dind-import: ${n_snap} committed snapshot(s) for ${n_loaded} image(s)"
+[ "${n_snap}" -ge "${n_loaded}" ] || { echo "GA dind-import: ERROR: ${n_snap} snapshots for ${n_loaded} images -- images were not unpacked" >&2; exit 1; }
+
 # Tag the Supervisor how the OS expects it to be tagged.
 # GA: the GA launcher (haos-supervisor, patch 0130) runs
 # ghcr.io/greenautarky/<arch>-hassio-supervisor:latest -- never the upstream
diff --git a/buildroot-external/package/hassio/hassio.mk b/buildroot-external/package/hassio/hassio.mk
--- a/buildroot-external/package/hassio/hassio.mk
+++ b/buildroot-external/package/hassio/hassio.mk
@@ -177,6 +177,8 @@
 	# dind-import-containers.sh fails unless exactly this many load.
 	$(Q)echo $$(( $(words $(HASSIO_GA_IMAGES)) + $(if $(HASSIO_ADDON_IMAGES_JSON),$$(jq -r '.addons | length' $(HASSIO_ADDON_IMAGES_JSON)),0) )) > $(@D)/images.expected
 	@echo "GA hassio: data partition must carry $$(cat $(@D)/images.expected) image(s)"
+	# GA (Odoo #2067): the board arch the images are unpacked for (dind-import-containers.sh maps it to the platform)
+	$(Q)echo $(call qstrip,$(BR2_PACKAGE_HASSIO_ARCH)) > $(@D)/images.arch
 endef
 
 # /etc/ga-version-url: the haos-version base URL the device POLLS, written from
